1
00:00:01,540 --> 00:00:02,400
Hello there!

2
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:08,157
Things have finally calmed down,
probably because it's so late at night.

3
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:10,857
There's nothing to do and no
one to talk to at this hour.

4
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:14,377
I guess I could check on my stats
since I haven't done that in a while.

5
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:17,417
Maybe I'll start by reviewing
all my vending machine types.

6
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,557
Vending machines are largely
divided into two categories.

7
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:23,957
Those that sell goods, and
those with automated services.

8
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:26,137
The first category is
pretty self-explanatory.

9
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:28,640
Those machines sell all kinds of things.

10
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:32,577
Even just within the food and drink
category, you've got sodas, coffee, alcohol,

11
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:35,657
milk drinks, candy, cooking
products, frozen desserts, etc.

12
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:37,877
Then there are cigarettes,
tickets, postcards,

13
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:39,857
postage stamps of all kinds, newspapers,

14
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:41,293
magazines, you name it.

15
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:44,117
It's gonna be another one.

16
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:45,030
Hello there.

17
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:46,650
All right.

18
00:00:46,733 --> 00:00:47,676
Thank you very much.

19
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:52,197
Next, you've got automated service
machines, which include all kinds of stuff,

20
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:54,897
like money-changing machines
and pachinko ball dispensers.

21
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:57,137
There's been intense
discourse over whether these

22
00:00:57,220 --> 00:00:59,057
automated service units
are vending machines?

23
00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:02,337
But in my opinion if you pay a
machine to vend a thing it counts!

24
00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:04,797
That must be why power
washer is in my function

25
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:07,317
list and I only just
recently noticed this.

26
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:09,900
But rank 3 has been added to that list.

27
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:14,377
I guess that means I still have room to
grow in my journey as a vending machine

28
00:01:14,460 --> 00:01:17,500
To attain rank 3 I would
need 3 million points.

29
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:20,257
I don't even know what
that would let me do

30
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:21,297
But I'm grateful.

31
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:23,733
I get to chase my vending machine dreams

32
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:26,880
Having goals makes me so happy.

33
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:37,960
Yeah, I know it's fried chicken,

34
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:42,394
but I can't pronounce it well so fried
chicken is what ended up sticking!

35
00:01:46,140 --> 00:01:47,580
Alright, alright relax.

36
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:49,468
There's plenty to go around

37
00:01:55,860 --> 00:02:00,657
On the outside, I'm just a big metal box,
but inside, I've still got a human soul.

38
00:02:00,740 --> 00:02:01,917
In this new world of wonders,

39
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,937
I travel to and fro on the back
of my super strong partner,

40
00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:05,850
Lamas.

41
00:02:05,933 --> 00:02:07,920
The name's Boxo. Hello there.

42
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:09,880
That means yes, by the way.

43
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:27,577
Hume and me stayed up all night
fixing the transfer circle,

44
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:31,197
so we've started evacuating the
residents of the Origin Stratum.

45
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:34,692
Their place of refuge will be
the Clear Flow Lake Stratum.

46
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:39,294
Come to think of it, I still don't
know how many strata this dungeon has.

47
00:03:42,820 --> 00:03:43,857
Horwa many?

48
00:03:43,940 --> 00:03:45,528
Oh, right, how many strata?

49
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:47,547
Well, starting from the top,

50
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:49,357
there's the Origin Stratum,

51
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:54,140
the Dead's Lament Stratum, Clear Flow
Lake Stratum, The Labyrinth Stratum,

52
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:59,580
Scorching Sand Stratum, Dark Forest
Stratum, and then Dog Mountain Stratum.

53
00:04:00,020 --> 00:04:01,040
That's not all.

54
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:05,077
Below that is the Everlasting
Stratum, which is yet to be conquered.

55
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:09,100
So at this point, we know there
are at least eight stratum.

56
00:04:09,260 --> 00:04:11,378
Alright, let's begin the evacuation.

57
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:30,137
Well, the transfer circle
seems to be working just fine.

58
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:32,837
Raises the question, what
do we do with it after this?

59
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:35,597
If we just abandon it and
the monsters misuse it,

60
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:37,917
it'll cause a lot of
trouble for other strata.

61
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,077
We could hunt down the
Netherlord's underling

62
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:42,057
and break their control over the monsters.

63
00:04:42,140 --> 00:04:43,837
That would solve the problem.

64
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:44,750
Theoretically, yes.

65
00:04:44,833 --> 00:04:48,017
But I can't afford to spare the manpower
it would require to hunt them down.

66
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:50,937
Well, in that case, how about
trusting the hunting parts,

67
00:04:51,020 --> 00:04:53,877
the esteemed menagerie of
fools and band of gluttons.

68
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:56,377
Does he think being
dashing will have his case?

69
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:57,797
You're willing to do that?

70
00:04:57,880 --> 00:04:58,821
I'd be happy to.

71
00:04:58,980 --> 00:05:01,980
I want to gather more info
on the Neverborn anyway.

72
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:04,460
That said, it's going to cost you.

73
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:06,010
Fair enough.

74
00:05:06,260 --> 00:05:08,966
The better the results,
the higher the reward.

75
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:12,762
He was going to do it even
if she refused to pay.

76
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:22,977
Mishuel's really got the moves, huh, Akka?

77
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:25,942
Yeah, sure wish we had a
flashy attack like that.

78
00:05:31,320 --> 00:05:34,680
Oh, water, become Whirlpools and fear!

79
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:40,718
Incredible fighting there, everyone.

80
00:05:41,140 --> 00:05:44,611
Boxxo, might I trouble you for
a little something to drink?

81
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:48,920
You're not fighting?

82
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:54,980
No, seeing how my primary function is
healing, I have no arsenal of offensive magic,

83
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:58,097
which essentially means I
am a bystander in combat.

84
00:05:58,180 --> 00:06:00,239
We each have our own roles to play.

85
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:02,558
I'm not sure if he's serious or not.

86
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:05,311
Heavy's face is particularly hard to read.

87
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:08,560
Now, which way do we go?

88
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:12,757
The map says there's a small
lake not far ahead to the right.

89
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:15,637
On the other hand, if we
go left, it's a long haul,

90
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:18,457
and there's a three-way
split in the path from there.

91
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:22,217
I think we should check out the
lake first, but from there, uh...

92
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:23,180
What's that?

93
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:27,892
Can't we just pause to chat
without some jerks showing up?

94
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:29,390
Huh?

95
00:06:29,473 --> 00:06:30,437
Heavy, what are you doing?

96
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:32,237
It's dangerous to get that close!

97
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:33,240
Pay it no mind.

98
00:06:33,540 --> 00:06:34,777
Heavy, hold your horses!

99
00:06:34,860 --> 00:06:35,690
Fret not, Captain.

100
00:06:35,773 --> 00:06:37,380
I'll handle this. Okay, fine.

101
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:38,370
Suit yourself.

102
00:06:43,420 --> 00:06:44,596
What's up with that?

103
00:06:44,780 --> 00:06:46,721
What are they looking around for?

104
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:48,900
Why aren't the monsters attacking?

105
00:06:50,420 --> 00:06:54,700
I'll bet they might see walls that
are invisible to us. That's correct.

106
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:57,657
Heavy excels in magic
that manipulates light.

107
00:06:57,740 --> 00:06:59,297
This allows him to produce illusions,

108
00:06:59,380 --> 00:07:02,615
and he's also able to influence
the mind more directly.

109
00:07:03,020 --> 00:07:03,850
Oh, right.

110
00:07:03,933 --> 00:07:06,388
Like when he hid those
people in the prison.

111
00:07:09,660 --> 00:07:14,940
I have no interest in those who go
barefoot, so there's no need to spare these.

112
00:07:16,260 --> 00:07:18,260
He has the blessing of might too,

113
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:21,500
though I will say it's not
as strong as Llama says.

114
00:07:24,820 --> 00:07:26,240
Whoa, no mercy!

115
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:29,541
I think it's safe to say
Heavy's got this handled.

116
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:39,557
Right, I think we should
split up into two groups.

117
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:42,077
It would be pretty dumb if we
all searched in one direction

118
00:07:42,160 --> 00:07:44,937
and they got past us just by
coming from the other way.

119
00:07:45,020 --> 00:07:48,517
If it's all the same to you, Captain,
I wish to accompany the lake group.

120
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:50,718
All right, where should we go, Boxo?

121
00:07:51,020 --> 00:07:53,937
Hmm, I'm concerned for
everyone in the heavy group.

122
00:07:54,020 --> 00:07:55,540
If I had to choose...

123
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:57,577
That took way.

124
00:07:57,660 --> 00:07:59,680
Oh, you want to go to the lake?

125
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:00,919
Sure, sounds good.

126
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:04,199
Alrighty then, Captain,
we're going to the lake too.

127
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:10,080
Good grief.

128
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:12,797
This search party only
includes half our members,

129
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:15,397
but we managed to wipe
these guys out in no time.

130
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:18,620
Wow, the lake water's
crystal clear. My friends,

131
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:20,917
we seem to be making excellent time,

132
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,235
so why don't you all take a
break and get in the water?

133
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:25,277
Ugh, majorly sus.

134
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:27,077
The others are waiting on us,

135
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:29,777
so we'd better hurry back
the captain said we needed to

136
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:32,777
be back in about three hours
And we're well within that.

137
00:08:32,860 --> 00:08:33,690
Yeah, you're right.

138
00:08:33,773 --> 00:08:34,677
He did say that.

139
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:37,466
I don't know you guys
can stand there debating

140
00:08:38,880 --> 00:08:40,160
Yeah, I'm with you

141
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:49,377
No, they seem tempted to
join in danger ladies.

142
00:08:49,460 --> 00:08:50,620
Don't worry girls.

143
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:54,917
I will be right here on the shore standing
guard I think even just dipping your

144
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,077
feet in the water and washing your hair
would make you feel quite refreshed.

145
00:08:58,160 --> 00:09:01,460
Yeah, that sounds nice.
Want to, Lamas? Well, okay.

146
00:09:01,740 --> 00:09:03,357
A little dip can't hurt, right?

147
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:05,060
Wait here for a bit, Boxo.

148
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:08,570
And...

149
00:09:08,653 --> 00:09:09,483
form change!

150
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:11,910
Oh, my.

151
00:09:12,180 --> 00:09:14,062
This is no place to leave these.

152
00:09:14,260 --> 00:09:16,613
Someone might come along and steal them.

153
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:19,641
I had better keep an eye
out while the girls swim.

154
00:09:20,120 --> 00:09:24,037
Though I can't help but wonder,
what do both their shoes smell like?

155
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:25,900
I called it! Too bad!

156
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:31,261
Saw that coming from a mile away.

157
00:09:32,020 --> 00:09:34,726
Why don't you get some
refreshment too, Heavy?

158
00:09:34,940 --> 00:09:37,528
And wash your dirty
mind while you're at it.

159
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:40,940
Hey, we're back! Hi there!

160
00:09:41,580 --> 00:09:43,120
Oh, glad to see you all.

161
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:45,397
Um, Heavy, why are you soaking wet?

162
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:48,539
I just fell in the lake for
purely personal reasons.

163
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:50,908
I'm leaving that one alone.

164
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:54,680
I believe it's about time for lunch.

165
00:09:55,060 --> 00:09:56,200
Boxo, if you would.

166
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:57,700
I'd be happy to.

167
00:09:57,960 --> 00:10:02,372
In fact, I want to try out a new function
I think you guys will appreciate.

168
00:10:02,580 --> 00:10:03,620
Form change!

169
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:06,777
It's a vending machine
market where you can

170
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:09,331
buy convenient store items 24 hours a day.

171
00:10:09,420 --> 00:10:13,596
And I get to show off my knack for
arranging things with limited space.

172
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:16,417
Okay, so here's the ideal lineup.

173
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:20,840
Come taste the wonders of a vending
machine-turned-mini-convenient store!

174
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:22,430
Wow!

175
00:10:22,513 --> 00:10:24,157
That is a treasure trove of delight!

176
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:26,797
Yeah, there are foods in there
I've never even heard of before!

177
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:29,351
That means I'll just have to try them all!

178
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:34,997
Seriously, it all looks
freaking delicious!

179
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:37,557
Yes, we will have to sample
everything, won't we?

180
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:38,877
Where should we start, Akka?

181
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:42,489
Let's each choose different
items and then go halfsy, Shiro!

182
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:49,320
Oh wait, they probably don't know how to
open a rice ball, so I should demonstrate.

183
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:56,140
Pardon me, comrades?

184
00:10:57,520 --> 00:11:02,060
I do apologize, but like that,
can I get some help over here?

185
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:05,640
I'm fatiguing and alarming right here.

186
00:11:06,820 --> 00:11:08,097
Boxo, Boxo.

187
00:11:08,180 --> 00:11:09,140
Boxo.

188
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:13,770
Hold it!

189
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:16,981
We'll probably find them
somewhere down this hill.

190
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:18,520
Yes, most likely.

191
00:11:18,940 --> 00:11:22,352
Mishuel, can you tell how many
beings might be down there?

192
00:11:23,120 --> 00:11:26,017
They're too close together
for me to count accurately.

193
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:29,237
That being said, we should be
prepared for at least a hundred.

194
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:31,140
Oh, that's all? Good.

195
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:34,097
We won't get our butts handed to
us even if we charge right in.

196
00:11:34,180 --> 00:11:36,037
Mishuel, you and I will take the lead.

197
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:37,277
Yeah, that's fine by me.

198
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:39,180
Is there anything I can do?

199
00:11:39,940 --> 00:11:42,320
Could I slow down the monsters somehow?

200
00:11:43,460 --> 00:11:45,040
Oh, I know just the thing!

201
00:11:45,780 --> 00:11:46,700
Form change!

202
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:49,400
Oh, Boxo, what's going on?

203
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:57,320
This is kind of incredible!

204
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:03,317
Master Boxo, can you tell
me what these balls are?

205
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:05,576
Too close for comfort there, Mishuel.

206
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:08,190
So then,

207
00:12:08,273 --> 00:12:11,597
if they try to charge, they'll just slip
on these little balls and fall down?

208
00:12:11,680 --> 00:12:12,540
Cut off. Act.

209
00:12:13,180 --> 00:12:16,415
We should declare Lamas the
official Boxxo interpreter.

210
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:20,557
I think I hear monsters
screaming from that way.

211
00:12:20,640 --> 00:12:22,977
They sound weird, though,
and there's lots of noise.

212
00:12:23,060 --> 00:12:23,890
Good.

213
00:12:23,973 --> 00:12:25,717
Seems like Boxxo set the stage for us.

214
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:27,137
Let's get in there, people!

215
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:28,050
Yes, sir!

216
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:30,586
If there's this many of them,

217
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:33,217
I bet the commander's in there somewhere!

218
00:12:33,300 --> 00:12:34,535
Let the battle begin!

219
00:12:35,300 --> 00:12:36,182
Roaring strike!

220
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:41,697
If I could only grow to
be as strong as Mishuel,

221
00:12:41,780 --> 00:12:45,721
I just know I'd be a lot more help
to everyone in times like these.

222
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:49,160
You're fine, Lamas.

223
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:52,197
Right, I'd better get busy. Recently,

224
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:54,597
I realized I can switch out
goods to get access to this

225
00:12:54,680 --> 00:12:57,677
candy without turning into the
specialized vending machine.

226
00:12:57,760 --> 00:13:00,289
You never know these
things unless you try.

227
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:01,610
Launch!

228
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:09,997
Boxxo, can you maybe handle
the enemies behind us?

229
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:10,910
Hello there!

230
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:13,897
Letting me cover her back
is proof that she trusts me.

231
00:13:13,980 --> 00:13:16,180
It's a man's job to live up to that!

232
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:19,720
I now know that this works
great as a blunt weapon.

233
00:13:19,940 --> 00:13:24,469
So I'll use it to take out any enemy
that tries to attack llamas from behind.

234
00:13:25,940 --> 00:13:26,820
Glory! Strike!

235
00:13:31,260 --> 00:13:32,517
They just keep coming.

236
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:36,197
We can't win if new guys keep showing
up as fast as we can take them out.

237
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:38,217
We need to locate the commander somehow.

238
00:13:38,300 --> 00:13:40,177
I might as well try asking Lamas.

239
00:13:40,260 --> 00:13:42,620
Lam is... You called? Ah!

240
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:45,720
Us, the people, they're there!

241
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:49,197
Uh, wait, you want me
to throw you over there?

242
00:13:49,280 --> 00:13:50,757
No way! I can't!

243
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:52,917
I don't want to use you like
you're just some object!

244
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,880
You're a-perton-er. Partner?

245
00:13:57,980 --> 00:13:59,517
Yeah, we are partners, huh?

246
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:02,188
Well, as your partner,
allow me to say this.

247
00:14:02,740 --> 00:14:03,570
No!

248
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:04,610
Oh!

249
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:09,317
Voxor, are you trying to put yourself
in harm's way out of concern for me?

250
00:14:09,400 --> 00:14:11,282
Here I am, doing the same thing.

251
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:14,657
I never want you to get hurt,
and I'd do anything to stop it.

252
00:14:14,740 --> 00:14:16,060
Yeah, you're right.

253
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:18,070
Suori, be!

254
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:19,395
No need to apologize.

255
00:14:19,740 --> 00:14:21,860
Our hearts beat as one after all.

256
00:14:22,040 --> 00:14:23,800
I attack, and you defend!

257
00:14:24,160 --> 00:14:26,200
Together, we can do anything! Yes!

258
00:14:26,840 --> 00:14:28,237
From now on, we'll work together.

259
00:14:28,320 --> 00:14:31,317
We'll determine a suitable
strategy for every situation.

260
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:33,157
And so, let's work together now.

261
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:34,997
We can launch a suicide attack!

262
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:36,737
I'm sorry, did I hear you right?

263
00:14:36,820 --> 00:14:39,349
I think that's a little
extreme, don't you?

264
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:44,976
Lamas, Master Boxo, if you're coming
through, allow me to clear a path.

265
00:14:47,140 --> 00:14:49,200
Master Boxo, feel free to proceed.

266
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:51,260
No, you feel free to stop us.

267
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:54,797
Thanks, Mishuel, that's Boxo's
number one offenses for you.

268
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:56,917
Oh, please, no need for flattery.

269
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,529
Fishwell seems bolstered
by the compliment.

270
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:01,240
Welp, here goes nothing!

271
00:15:05,580 --> 00:15:10,220
To incapacitate enemies without defeating
them, that calls for pachinko balls.

272
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:14,960
The best product for slipping and
falling would have to be these. Launch!

273
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:22,080
Hey, this is kind of fun!

274
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:24,040
More balls coming at ya!

275
00:15:28,220 --> 00:15:29,050
Nice.

276
00:15:29,133 --> 00:15:30,512
That takes care of them.

277
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:32,377
Boxxo, where's the commander?

278
00:15:32,460 --> 00:15:33,820
It's all green fiends.

279
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,057
I don't see anything that
looks like a commander.

280
00:15:36,140 --> 00:15:36,970
Boxxo!

281
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,220
What the heck?

282
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:48,340
Mikenne! You okay? What happened?
Thanks, Slomus. Hey, listen.

283
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:52,756
Before, I heard what sounded like
human screams coming from over there.

284
00:15:52,980 --> 00:15:54,921
I think it was inside that mound.

285
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:58,420
There's still faint moans
coming out of it. Oh, good.

286
00:15:58,660 --> 00:16:00,637
That first attack must have done the job.

287
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:02,860
In that case, form change!

288
00:16:03,700 --> 00:16:04,820
Power washer!

289
00:16:07,740 --> 00:16:09,020
There and there, huh?

290
00:16:09,180 --> 00:16:10,517
Okay, I'll go check it out.

291
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:12,580
You wait right here. Good luck!

292
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:18,710
There!

293
00:16:19,780 --> 00:16:22,040
Oh, there's the commander! Good!

294
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:27,631
When all your attacks can't
stop them, you go for the ring.

295
00:16:31,180 --> 00:16:33,356
That's one less thing to worry about.

296
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:37,791
Master Boxo, we cleared a path of retreat.

297
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:39,805
Right, go back to the pathway.

298
00:16:40,920 --> 00:16:44,177
Now, since we've made it this
far, that's mission accomplished.

299
00:16:44,260 --> 00:16:47,377
With Kerioyl here, we'll question
her once we get back to the village.

300
00:16:47,460 --> 00:16:48,337
Yes, we will.

301
00:16:48,420 --> 00:16:50,397
But should you be taking advantage of this

302
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:52,817
trying situation by
patting a woman's rear?

303
00:16:52,900 --> 00:16:53,730
Hey, relax.

304
00:16:53,813 --> 00:16:54,643
I was just caught up in the moment.

305
00:16:54,726 --> 00:16:55,556
That's all.

306
00:16:55,639 --> 00:16:56,937
It's not like I
premeditated it or anything.

307
00:16:57,020 --> 00:16:58,200
You sure about that?

308
00:16:58,420 --> 00:17:00,714
Those two are really adorable together.

309
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:04,277
What exactly is their
relationship, anyway?

310
00:17:04,360 --> 00:17:05,937
Captain, you always act like this.

311
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:06,850
As vice-captain...

312
00:17:06,933 --> 00:17:09,417
Aren't they too old to be fighting
like this in front of everyone, Akka?

313
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:10,330
Probably so.

314
00:17:10,520 --> 00:17:12,697
It's always so embarrassing
to watch, isn't it?

315
00:17:12,780 --> 00:17:14,337
What does he mean, too old?

316
00:17:14,420 --> 00:17:16,597
Isn't Vice-Captain Phil
Mina pretty young, though?

317
00:17:16,680 --> 00:17:18,386
Oh, you mean you didn't know?

318
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:21,617
She might look young, but she's
older than the captain, actually.

319
00:17:21,700 --> 00:17:22,530
What?

320
00:17:22,613 --> 00:17:23,757
There's just no way that's true.

321
00:17:23,840 --> 00:17:28,160
Oh, well, the vice-captain is half
some race, one I can't remember now.

322
00:17:28,420 --> 00:17:30,717
The race in question is vamp fiend, Shui.

323
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:31,700
Vamp fiend?

324
00:17:31,860 --> 00:17:33,657
I've never even heard of that race.

325
00:17:33,740 --> 00:17:34,570
Hold on.

326
00:17:34,653 --> 00:17:35,617
From what I understand,

327
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:38,977
vamp fiends are the race that survive
by feeding on people's blood, right?

328
00:17:39,060 --> 00:17:41,577
And they're all beautiful creatures
who look just like humans?

329
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:44,837
Yes, and to add to that, vamp fiends
may get nourishment in other ways.

330
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:48,802
from bodily fluids whose composition
is somewhat similar to blood.

331
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:53,537
Which is why it isn't uncommon for them
to bond with humans and have children.

332
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:54,600
Or so I believe.

333
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:56,600
So romantic!

334
00:17:56,980 --> 00:17:58,897
Then those two are
destined for each other!

335
00:17:58,980 --> 00:18:01,277
The blood thing doesn't bother you at all?

336
00:18:01,360 --> 00:18:03,337
Lamas, that's being with a monster.

337
00:18:03,420 --> 00:18:05,067
Some call it an abomination.

338
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:08,397
Seems like that's not how they
thought Lamas would react.

339
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:09,310
So what?

340
00:18:09,393 --> 00:18:12,117
Just because someone's race or
appearance is different from your own,

341
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:14,377
that doesn't mean anything
about who they are as a person.

342
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:15,360
Right, Boxo?

343
00:18:15,540 --> 00:18:16,540
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

344
00:18:16,920 --> 00:18:19,317
And the Menagerie of
Fools has accepted her,

345
00:18:19,400 --> 00:18:21,597
so she's just the same as everyone else.

346
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:22,510
You're right.

347
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:24,875
We are a bunch of oddballs, aren't we?

348
00:18:26,220 --> 00:18:27,420
I just remembered.

349
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:31,137
Don't the Menagerie of Fools members
have a few wishes they want granted?

350
00:18:31,220 --> 00:18:34,338
Would it be okay for me to
ask what those wishes are?

351
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:37,917
Oh, sorry.

352
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,377
I forget there are things
people don't talk about.

353
00:18:40,460 --> 00:18:41,400
No, it's okay.

354
00:18:41,600 --> 00:18:42,937
I only have one wish.

355
00:18:43,020 --> 00:18:46,257
to make tons of money that I
can use to help the orphanage.

356
00:18:46,340 --> 00:18:48,417
My dream is for the
children and I to be able to

357
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:51,324
eat all the tasty food
we want every single day.

358
00:18:51,580 --> 00:18:54,109
Yeah, that's a simple, Shui kind of wish.

359
00:18:54,460 --> 00:18:56,460
I can share mine next if you want.

360
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:59,860
My one wish is to somehow
make Boxo human again.

361
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:01,120
Aw, that's sweet.

362
00:19:01,300 --> 00:19:04,217
Oh, does that mean that you and
Boxo share the same wish, cute?

363
00:19:04,300 --> 00:19:05,130
Yeah.

364
00:19:05,213 --> 00:19:07,902
I have a lot of them, but
we'll leave it at that.

365
00:19:08,040 --> 00:19:09,177
Since we're sharing,

366
00:19:09,260 --> 00:19:11,817
I have been yearning to share my
own deepest desire with you all.

367
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:13,135
No, thank you, Heavy.

368
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:15,040
Oh, that simply won't do.

369
00:19:15,260 --> 00:19:17,857
How uncouth would it be to listen
to my comrades pour out their

370
00:19:17,940 --> 00:19:21,177
souls while keeping my own feelings
locked away in my heart of hearts?

371
00:19:21,260 --> 00:19:24,017
My wish is to collect footwear
from all over the world?

372
00:19:24,100 --> 00:19:25,917
At the moment just before it wears out.

373
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:29,437
and use said footwear to construct
a vast and ornate castle.

374
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:31,637
And for the next phase of my dream plan,

375
00:19:31,720 --> 00:19:34,037
At the end of each year, I
shall tax my constituents?

376
00:19:34,120 --> 00:19:37,897
collecting footwear they've worn
throughout the preceding months.

377
00:19:37,980 --> 00:19:41,098
That is the most depraved
wish I've heard in a while.

378
00:19:42,300 --> 00:19:44,237
Well, I guess it's our turn next.

379
00:19:44,320 --> 00:19:47,177
You all probably know that Shiro and
I share a common wish as well, right?

380
00:19:47,260 --> 00:19:48,090
That's right, Akka.

381
00:19:48,173 --> 00:19:50,157
And so our most ardent wish is this.

382
00:19:50,240 --> 00:19:52,300
To be popular with the ladies!

383
00:19:53,540 --> 00:19:56,481
Well, that's rich coming
from a couple of virgins.

384
00:19:58,260 --> 00:19:59,090
Too bad.

385
00:19:59,460 --> 00:20:01,517
What about the captain and vice-captain?

386
00:20:01,600 --> 00:20:02,597
That I don't know.

387
00:20:02,680 --> 00:20:06,739
I asked them about it once upon a
time, but they dodged the question.

388
00:20:06,900 --> 00:20:07,841
Yeah, same here.

389
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:08,830
And here, too.

390
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:11,911
Every person has their secrets, after all.

391
00:20:12,120 --> 00:20:14,885
There is no sense in
trying to ferret them out.

392
00:20:15,020 --> 00:20:19,037
Heavy can be pretty insightful when
he's not being weird about shoes.

393
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:21,237
Alright, enough chit-chat, you guys.

394
00:20:21,320 --> 00:20:23,817
Hurry up if you want to get
back to the village today.

395
00:20:23,900 --> 00:20:24,730
Okay.

396
00:20:26,420 --> 00:20:28,008
Excellent work, all of you.

397
00:20:28,620 --> 00:20:32,817
Boxo, may I trouble you to provide us with
food and drinks for a celebratory feast?

398
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:33,730
Hello there.

399
00:20:35,500 --> 00:20:37,740
Oh, looks so good.

400
00:20:38,880 --> 00:20:40,040
I've been waiting!

401
00:20:40,380 --> 00:20:42,177
I'm so happy and fried chicken!

402
00:20:42,260 --> 00:20:43,090
Amazing!

403
00:20:43,740 --> 00:20:48,269
All right, now to attempt something I've
been wanting to try for a while now.

404
00:20:48,640 --> 00:20:49,600
Warm change!

405
00:20:49,980 --> 00:20:51,580
A rice vending machine!

406
00:20:52,380 --> 00:20:55,597
Now that I have telekinesis,
I can even prepare it myself.

407
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:57,240
At least I think so.

408
00:20:57,740 --> 00:20:59,580
Now, how will I cook this?

409
00:20:59,780 --> 00:21:01,560
Hey, Boxo, what's this stuff?

410
00:21:01,840 --> 00:21:04,200
It's cookery, right? I know!

411
00:21:06,080 --> 00:21:07,500
Please, help!

412
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:09,470
Mm-hmm. Sure.

413
00:21:09,620 --> 00:21:10,679
What should we do?

414
00:21:11,180 --> 00:21:12,080
Form change?

415
00:21:12,540 --> 00:21:14,020
A gas vending machine!

416
00:21:14,820 --> 00:21:17,840
Oh, eight. There! Like this? Thank you.

417
00:21:18,580 --> 00:21:21,200
Oh, this is a magic
item that produces fire.

418
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:25,920
I did get some help at the end, but
I think I can handle simple cooking.

419
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:29,740
But, Boxxo, why did you start
cooking all of a sudden?

420
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:31,313
That's a good question.

421
00:21:31,420 --> 00:21:33,949
You can already dispense
all kinds of food.

422
00:21:35,300 --> 00:21:37,947
How do I tell them I
tried it just for kicks?

423
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:41,880
And with that, the rice is done.

424
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,553
I'll go get some bowls.

425
00:21:43,640 --> 00:21:45,052
I'll help you with that.

426
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:47,920
This is so tasty!

427
00:21:48,320 --> 00:21:49,640
Yeah, tasty is right.

428
00:21:51,520 --> 00:21:53,755
All I did was cook using my abilities.

429
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:57,245
But I'm really satisfied
with myself right now.

430
00:21:57,600 --> 00:22:00,040
Oh, Boxo, thanks for all that you do.

431
00:22:01,280 --> 00:22:03,927
I think I might cook
again from time to time.

432
00:22:41,420 --> 00:22:44,160
I'll walk you through the same time.

433
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:46,120
How are you going?

434
00:22:47,520 --> 00:22:51,640
I'll be able to walk you
through the next day.

435
00:22:51,760 --> 00:22:53,760
I'll be able to change the future.

436
00:22:54,900 --> 00:22:58,460
This melody is the words of the road.

437
00:22:59,280 --> 00:23:00,377
We're moving on the way.

438
00:23:00,460 --> 00:23:04,120
I'll be able to keep my own life.

439
00:23:13,080 --> 00:23:15,397
See you

440
00:23:15,480 --> 00:23:20,120
next time.

441
00:23:34,900 --> 00:23:36,780
You could even win a reward.

442
00:23:37,840 --> 00:23:39,958
I look forward to serving you again.
